{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>When you come to the land of your dwelling-places.</b> Why is this passage juxtaposed to the passage of the spies? Because when Israel heard the decree of the Holy One, blessed be He, they said: Woe to us — we will never enter the land, for even after forty years, if we sin He will decree another decree, and so there is no end to the matter. The Holy One, blessed be He, said to them: You will surely come to the land after forty years."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:26.990469668Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}